Janis Papanagnou <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com> writes:

[about transferring bones in some generic format]

> Given the huge size of a XML transfer syntax you won't be able to
> avoid some compression (as already implemented); any compression

If there is any compression used, it should be something that is
guaranteed to be implemented on any platform that Nethack is ported to.
And there should be a free implementation for every platform, somewhere
that the users of that platform will know where to find it. Otherwise it
conflicts with the whole idea of platform-independent portable files.

But are you sure compression would be needed? The generic format would
only be needed for transferring the files from one platform to another, the
files would not be always stored in that format.
At least the compression wouldn't need to be integrated in the export /
import utilities. The files could be first imported, then packed (for
example with zip), transferred to the other machine, unpacked and imported
to that platform. 

